## 👥 Team Collaboration Problems

Without a source-driven workflow like Salesforce DX and GitHub, teams managing large multi-developer environments inevitably run into massive operational roadblocks:

### 1. Code Overwrites (The "Last-Saved Wins" Conflict)
When multiple developers work out of a shared sandbox or deploy directly to an upstream integration environment via change sets, they routinely overwrite each other's custom logic. A developer saving a modification to an Apex class or a page layout can unknowingly wipe out an entire week's worth of a teammate's changes.

### 2. The Sandbox Refresh Dilemma
Keeping developer sandboxes identical and in sync is nearly impossible in an org-centric model. Sandboxes drift out of sync almost immediately after creation, leading to situations where code passes perfectly in a local environment but fails unexpectedly during production deployments due to missing dependencies.

### 3. Change Set Management Hell
Manually assembling change sets is a tedious, error-prone task. Developers must scroll through hundreds of metadata lines in a web UI to click components one by one. If a single dependency is forgotten, the deployment fails, forcing the developer to clone the change set and start the uploading sequence all over again.

